Requirements & Prerequisites

Minimum Hardware (Development):
Component	          CPU	        RAM	    Disk	    Notes
Elasticsearch	    2 cores	        4GB	    20GB	    Must heap size 50% of RAM
Logstash	        1 core	        2GB	    10GB	    Heap size depends on pipeline
Kibana	            1 core	        1GB	    1GB	        Mostly static
Filebeat	        0.5 core	    256MB	1GB	        Per application server

Production Minimum (100GB logs/day):
Component	          CPU	        RAM	    Disk	    Count
Elasticsearch	    8 cores	        32GB	2TB SSD	    3 nodes minimum
Logstash	        4 cores	        8GB	    100GB SSD   (for queue)	2 nodes (HA)
Kibana	            2 cores	        2GB	    10GB	    1 + failover
Load Balancer	    1 core	        1GB	    N/A	        For ES/Kibana

Operating System Prerequisites (CRITICAL):
bash
# 1. Increase memory map count (or ES won't start)
sudo sysctl -w vm.max_map_count=262144
echo "vm.max_map_count=262144" >> /etc/sysctl.conf

# 2. Increase file descriptors
ulimit -n 65535
echo "elasticsearch soft nofile 65535" >> /etc/security/limits.conf
echo "elasticsearch hard nofile 65535" >> /etc/security/limits.conf

# 3. Disable swapping (performance killer)
sudo swapoff -a

# 4. Increase process limit
echo "elasticsearch soft nproc 4096" >> /etc/security/limits.conf

# 5. TCP tuning for high throughput
sysctl -w net.core.somaxconn=1024
sysctl -w net.ipv4.tcp_max_syn_backlog=4096
Software Prerequisites:
Java: Elasticsearch requires Java 11-17 (OpenJDK)

Docker (optional but common): Version 20.10+

Ports:

9200 (ES HTTP API)

9300 (ES internal cluster)

5044 (Filebeat → Logstash)

5601 (Kibana web UI)